@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: what must be green before publishing images, and where each part runs
' covers: mise.toml
' covers: e2e/gate_test.go
' covers: e2e/ladder_test.go
' covers: e2e/idle_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/base_template_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/release_gate_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/release_targets_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/retirement_test.go
' covers: internal/cdn/release/release.go
' covers: internal/maintain/e2e.go
' covers: internal/maintain/e2e_test.go
' covers: internal/maintain/e2e/main.go
' covers: internal/maintain/e2e/main_test.go
' Lineage and tags: image-lineage-and-publish.puml (same directory).
'
' ── THE RETIREMENT LEDGER BLOCKS A CLI RELEASE (N33, DONE (wt) 2026-10-18) ──
' A deprecated alias that promises to go "next release" needs something that
' notices the release happened. internal/contract/retirement_test.go holds a
' ledger of live retirements, each with a marker string. The four v0.2.0
' entries (two Go aliases, the egress/ run-root sweep, and the installer alias)
' were removed before the next release. The empty ledger stays active so new
' deprecations can be bounded. Tests:
'   TestEveryRetirementMarkerIsStillInTheTree  a ledger row whose marker is gone
'                                              must be deleted with it
'   TestEveryDeprecatedAliasHasARetirement     every envreg AliasOf has a row
'   TestNoRetirementOutlivesOneRelease         `git grep -F <marker> <prev>` at
'                                              the newest v* tag merged into
'                                              HEAD and not at HEAD; it fails
'                                              when that release already shipped
'                                              the marker
' A shallow clone has no tags to read, so the last test skips with a remedy.
' MEASURED 2026-10-18 on the release path of that day: the ledger ran before
' goreleaser and blocked the release unless it PASSED — a skip blocked too.
' Reported: red with a marker v0.1.2 contains, then green.
' Since 2026-11-17 `mise run deploy --cli` runs the ledger first, from Go
' (internal/cdn/release DefaultSteps): PROVEO_RELEASE_GATE=1 go test of
' TestNoRetirementOutlivesOneRelease. Under the gate, releaseGate(t) turns a
' skip into a failure. Without the gate the test skips in `mise run test`.
' The ledger runs before the question and before any git write, so a red
' ledger leaves HEAD, the tags and dist/ as they were. deploy --cli builds
' and stages from the pinned commit on origin/main. After verifying the
' live CDN manifest, it tags that same commit
' (_spec/internal/cdn/distribution-update.puml).
' HISTORY, 2026-11-12 to 2026-11-17: `mise run release` depended on a hidden
' release-ledger task that also ran TestReleaseShipsATaggedHead, so an
' untagged HEAD refused with `git tag vX.Y.Z`; deploy-cli's own run started
' with TestStagedCDNIsTheTaggedRelease because `mise run --skip-deps` drops
' depends (lab, mise 2026.10.17). A Go step has no depends to skip, and the
' tag check moved into release.StagedRefusal. A staging PR later enforced
' branch protection. The shared CI/local flow verifies the live manifest
' and publishes a tag for the approved source commit on main.
' The gate turned red after v0.2.0 shipped. Removing the expired surfaces
' and their ledger rows made HEAD eligible for the next release.
' MEASURED 2026-11-17: red again after v0.3.0 shipped proveo_retire_lsp_wiring;
' deleting it with its ledger row left the ledger empty.
' Notes here are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── THE GATE IS IN TWO HALVES, AND THAT IS NOT A CHOICE ─────────────────────
' A proveo sandbox has docker but NOT sbx: the CLI is in no proveo image, and
' /dev/kvm does not exist there with no kvm module loaded. So the sbx-backed
' checks cannot run where the rest of them do, and a release gate that lives
' only in one place would either skip them or refuse to run.
' The measurement and the NOT BUILT nested sbx:
' _spec/_paradigms/capability-ladder.puml (THE LADDER IS A HOST MEASUREMENT).
'
' IN-SANDBOX (or any host with docker):
'   1  go build ./... && go vet ./... && go vet -tags e2e ./e2e/
'      (`mise run lint` runs the e2e vet since 2026-11-10. A contract test,
'      TestProveoBuildsForEveryReleaseTarget, cross-builds cmd/proveo for the
'      eight goreleaser targets; `mise run ci` built the host platform only.)
'   2  go test ./...                     unit + contract
'   3  mise run build all                every image from source
'   4  mise run test-images              every TestImage* suite, hermes included —
'                                        the ONE image gate, maintain.ImageGatePlan;
'                                        mise run e2e runs it first unless
'                                        --no-images (N12, 2026-10-17;
'                                        TestOneImageTaskGatesBothReleaseGates).
'                                        HISTORY: "11 suites across all four defs",
'                                        and test-images-sbx skipped hermes.
'                                        It starts with a goreleaser snapshot, so
'                                        mise fetches goreleaser 2.17.0 (aqua,
'                                        GitHub releases) here. Nobody has measured
'                                        whether the sandbox's egress allows it.
'   5  go test -tags e2e ./e2e/          the non-sbx e2e suite
'
' ON THE HOST ONLY, because each needs sbx:
'   6  the ladder, PER DEF — one climb per target, not one climb:
'        mise run e2e --ladder [agent]...
'      maintain.E2EPlan plans one pass per picked agent: its own 30m process
'      with PROVEO_LADDER_TEST=1 and PROVEO_LADDER_TARGET=<agent>, running
'        go test -tags=e2e -count=1 -timeout 30m ./e2e/ -run=^TestSandboxLadder$ -v
'      maintain.RunE2E runs past a red pass and fails naming the red ones.
'      PROVEO_LADDER_TARGET stays singular. NOT CHOSEN: PROVEO_LADDER_TARGETS
'      with a subtest loop in one 120m process.
'      claudecode is the DEFAULT target, so a bare go test measures only it. The
'      sbx fixes this suite proved for claudecode were applied to cursor by
'      SYMMETRY rather than measurement — a contract with one data point.
'   7  the credential control:
'        PROVEO_SBX_AGENT_KIT=1 PROVEO_LADDER_TEST=1 \
'        go test -tags e2e ./e2e/ \
'          -run ProxyManagesTheCredential -v
'      It runs the SAME Kit twice, with and without credentials[], and fails if
'      both give the same value — so it proves the declaration CAUSES the
'      sentinel rather than merely coinciding with it.
'   8  silent-death idle, PER DEF:
'        mise run e2e --idle [agent]...
'      sets PROVEO_IDLE_TEST=1, PROVEO_IDLE_TARGETS=<picked ∩ claudecode,cursor,
'      opencode> and PROVEO_IDLE_FOR (45s when unset or blank) and runs
'      go test -run=^TestAgentSurvivesIdleAtPrompt$.
'      The ladder holds raw `sbx run`. Idle holds `proveo run`, where a leaked
'      DA1 becomes a prompt and the sandbox "was stopped". 45s is past sbx's
'      30s auto-stop and the ~14s cursor death; a SKIP is not a pass.
'   `mise run e2e --full` runs the image gate (red stops it), then the e2e
'   suite with PROVEO_IDLE_TEST and PROVEO_TOOLCHAIN_TEST on
'   (PROVEO_TEST_GO_TIMEOUT, 150m when unset or blank), then 8, then 6.
'   Every pass is its own go test process and runs past a red one; any red
'   pass fails the run ("red e2e passes: …"). --run reaches the suite alone.
'   NOT CHOSEN: one go test process for all passes (a timeout panic aborts
'   the rest). `mise run e2e --print` prints every pass's env and argv.
'   An agent named on the command line narrows idle and ladder; with none
'   named, an agent pass on a terminal opens a choiceui checklist with every
'   agent ticked, and a run without a terminal takes them all.
'   DECIDED 2026-11-17: one `e2e` task (the operator named it against the
'   test-* prefix) with --idle, --ladder, --toolchain, --full, --no-images,
'   --run and --print, planned by maintain.E2EPlan in internal/maintain/e2e.go.
'   HISTORY, until 2026-11-17: test-e2e-full ran `mise run --continue-on-error
'   e2e-gated ::: idle-all ::: ladder-all` (later test-idle and test-ladder),
'   and ladder-all ran hidden ladder:<def> tasks with --jobs=1. NOT CHOSEN
'   then: depends_post, a run array (it stops at the first failure) and
'   raw_args; the Go orchestrator replaced the whole composition.
'
' ── THE VERDICT ITSELF IS A THING THAT CAN BE WRONG ─────────────────────────
' HISTORY, until 2026-11-12: `ladder-all` (now `e2e --ladder`) read the ladder's result out of
' `go test` output, and it misread it twice, in OPPOSITE directions:
'
'   1  a SKIP exits 0, so an unchecked exit status reported PASS for four defs
'      on a host with no sbx — four climbs that never happened, certified.
'   2  the fix grepped for "--- SKIP: TestSandboxLadder" UNANCHORED, which also
'      matches the four-space-indented SUBTEST line. A def that passed every
'      rung with only its browser rung skipped was reported as not-run.
'
' Go prints the top-level result flush left and indents subtests, so the anchor
' was the whole correctness of the line: `'^--- SKIP: TestSandboxLadder [(]'`,
' against the two shapes verbatim from real runs:
'
'   ran, one rung skipped   --- PASS: TestSandboxLadder (168.93s)
'                               --- SKIP: TestSandboxLadder/2-proveo-browser-image (0.14s)
'   never ran                   ladder_test.go:314: sbx not available: sbx not on PATH
'                           --- SKIP: TestSandboxLadder (0.00s)
'
' ── THE VERDICT IS go test's EXIT CODE (2026-11-12) ─────────────────────────
' The Go verdict parsers that replaced the mise bash on 2026-09-22 are deleted
' with their dispatcher on 2026-11-12 (_spec/cmd/proveo/usage.puml). The
' opted-in tests now fail instead of skip:
' e2e/gate_test.go failSkipsWhenOptedIn(t, optIn) registers a t.Cleanup that
' fails t when t.Skipped() while the switch is on (envflag words). NOT CHOSEN:
' a gateSkip helper in place of each t.Skip, which misses a future bare skip.
' TestSandboxLadder calls it right after its PROVEO_LADDER_TEST opt-out, so a
' top-level skip (requireDocker, sbx) fails while a rung subtest's skip stays
' a skip. idleAtPrompt calls it first for PROVEO_IDLE_TEST, so a def whose
' sbx, image or credential is missing fails. go test's exit code is then the
' verdict, and maintain.RunE2E composes it per pass. go test -v streams the
' rung logs live.
' MEASURED 2026-11-12 with no docker or sbx on PATH: PROVEO_LADDER_TEST=1
' TestSandboxLadder exits 1 with "docker not available" and "PROVEO_LADDER_TEST
' is on, so this skip fails the gate"; PROVEO_IDLE_TEST=1 idle exits 1 the
' same way; without the switch both SKIP and exit 0.
' Pinned by TestOptedInE2EGatesFailTheirSkips and TestE2EIsTheOneE2ETask
' (base_template_test.go), TestE2EPlanFullIsTheSilentDeathGate
' (internal/maintain/e2e_test.go), and TestOptInTurnsASkipIntoAFailure
' (e2e/gate_test.go).
' --full sets PROVEO_IDLE_TEST=1 for the whole suite pass, so inside
' `e2e --full` the default claudecode idle check fails without sbx.
' PROVEO_SIGNAL_TEST=1 left the env 2026-10-16 with e2e/signal_test.go, whose
' subject — tearing down the docker egress sidecars on SIGINT — was deleted.
'
' ── WHAT A GREEN GATE DOES NOT COVER ────────────────────────────────────────
' Stated because a checklist read as complete is worse than one read as partial:
'
'   amd64.  Every measurement in this branch is arm64. `deploy` pushes
'     amd64+arm64, so the publish is the first amd64 compile. The node tarball
'     picks per-arch with a pinned sha256 for each and the purge is dpkg, so it
'     is arch-independent BY INSPECTION — which is not a build.
'
'   the first-run consent prompt. With PROVEO_SBX_AGENT_KIT defaulted on, sbx
'     asks before injecting a service the operator has not yet bound — once per
'     service, recorded in ~/.config/sbx/credentials.yaml, and it asks even for
'     a credential it already holds. An UNATTENDED agent stops there. No test
'     covers it because it is interactive by definition.
'
'   HISTORY: TestProjectDotEnvAtEgressLayer/opencode was RED and unexplained
'     on the docker backend. It was deleted 2026-10-16 with that backend, so
'     the question it raised is closed by removal, not answered.
'
' ── HISTORY: LEAKED STATE POISONED THE RESULT, AND HID FOR HOURS ────────────
' Docker-backend era; the -egress containers and *-mitm-net networks it names
' no longer exist. The rule — match on the image, never the name — stands.
' Two proveo/opencode:local containers ran for SIX HOURS after the sessions
' that started them were killed, each holding a *-mitm-net network. They were
' invisible to `docker ps -a | grep proveo` because docker had named them
' `romantic_haibt` and `tender_rhodes` — proveo starts them without --name, so
' MATCH ON THE IMAGE, NEVER THE NAME:
'     docker ps -a --filter ancestor=proveo/opencode:local
' Removing them changed the dotenv failure from a 5m timeout to "session exited
' before a new -egress container", which is a different and more useful fault.
' The underlying defect is a teardown that does not run when a session is
' killed; cmd/proveo/clean.go exists for it and nothing invoked it.
' ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

title Release gate — two halves, because sbx is host-only

node "in-sandbox · docker only" as BOX <<host>> {
  component "build + vet + go test" as GO <<app>>
  component "build all\n14 images from source" as BUILD <<app>>
  component "test-images\nevery TestImage* · hermes included\n(the one image task, N12)" as TI <<app>>
  component "e2e minus sbx" as E2E <<app>>
}

node "host only · needs sbx" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "e2e --idle × 3 agents\nproveo run · zero input" as IDLE <<db>>
  component "e2e --ladder × 4 agents\nclaudecode codex cursor opencode" as LAD <<db>>
  component "credential control\nsame Kit, with and without" as CRED <<db>>
}

component "deploy all\namd64 + arm64 --push\nthen untag :local" as PUB <<cloud>>
component "not covered\namd64 · consent prompt\n(the e2e never approves: SEC3)" as GAP <<error>>

GO ARROW_MAIN BUILD
BUILD ARROW_MAIN TI
TI ARROW_MAIN E2E
E2E ARROW_MAIN IDLE : hand off to the host
IDLE ARROW_MAIN LAD
LAD ARROW_MAIN CRED
CRED ARROW_MAIN PUB : only now
GAP ARROW_ERROR PUB : known blind spots

note bottom of HOST
  **Idle is the other host half.** The
  ladder holds raw ""sbx run""; idle
  holds ""proveo run"", where the DA1
  leak lives. ""e2e --full"" runs
  both, per agent. A SKIP is not a pass.
end note

note right of LAD
  **One climb per def, not one climb.**
  The target defaults to claudecode, so
  a bare run measures a fourth of the
  fleet. ""e2e --ladder"" climbs all four,
  one 30m process each.
end note

note bottom of LAD
  **An opted-in skip fails the climb.** A skip
  once exited 0 and read as a pass. Now a
  top-level skip under PROVEO_LADDER_TEST
  fails at cleanup; a rung skip stays a skip.
end note

note bottom of GAP
  **A checklist read as complete is worse than
  one read as partial.** amd64 has never been
  compiled here, and the consent prompt is
  interactive by definition.
end note

note bottom of TI
  **It prefers :local and PULLS otherwise.** A
  suite run without building first tested a
  seven-day-old published image and reported
  success — build all comes first for that
  reason, not for tidiness.
end note

note bottom of CRED
  **It proves causation, not coincidence.** The
  same Kit runs twice, with the credentials
  block and without, and an identical result
  either way fails the test.
end note

@enduml
